    "methods_description": "EEG recordings were conducted in a sound-isolating booth using a Brain Products system in BrainVision format. Stimuli were presented via ER-2 insert earphones for air conduction and a B-81 vibrator for bone conduction, controlled through an RME Digiface USB interface and custom Python scripts using expyfun. The pABR paradigm employed tone pips (500, 1000, 2000, 4000, 8000 Hz) presented at 40 Hz stimulation rate for air conduction (dichotic) and bone conduction (with contralateral masking at 400 Hz) across intensity levels of 20, 40, 50, 60, 70, and 30 dB peSPL. Behavioral data were collected using eye-tracking equipment with stimulus presentation rates of 20, 40, 60, and 80 Hz.",
